; The stage-1 blockout: one room with a balcony over its right half and a flight of stairs,
; standing on an island of grass of no particular shape, with trees and shrubs about it.
; Every grid row is exactly 32 cells wide; a space is a cell with no module — the island's
; edge is drawn round the map's outline (FR-MAP-200), and ',' is its ground.
; The room is shifted 4 cells across and 4 down from its old place, with doorways two
; cells wide west and south: the snake's body is wider than one (ADR-0021).
; The flight rises east along rows 15 and 16, eight steps of 0.375 m, into an opening
; three cells wide in the balcony's west wall (FR-MAP-150, ADR-0033).
; The partition in column 14 is a wall with a doorway two cells wide in rows 10 and 11; no tree
; stands one cell from a wall, at the island's edge, or corner to corner with the water; and two
; rows lie between the flight and the south wall. Each of those would be a way the map shows and
; the snake cannot take, which is refused (FR-MAP-260).
; The arena stands on Greenholm, an island (FR-MAP-120, FR-GREENHOLM-010).

